# C30 remediation after attempt-02 (8/7/8/7/7, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 cached record conflated with in-flight context bookkeeping | `OverviewRecord` keeps `parts: Vec<ContextRef>` (one per admitted read part, with its context) instead of one context and a counter; "reading" means a part under the current context is open; a part under a retired context is withdrawn when it lands (removed, never recorded, never counted); a current part completes the read only when no current part remains. `record_for` no longer takes a context. Test: `ui_v2_inbox::a_read_held_open_across_a_switch_round_trip_never_leaves_the_tenant_reading` (the key inventory held open by the plane; A → B → A; snooze and read again; generations count only valid completions; Read now keeps working) | `observation_domain.rs` |
| R2 listings counted complete when merely present | A listing establishes its source only when its page is the inventory (`complete`: not capped, nothing beyond the page); otherwise it is unread coverage. `ProductOutcome.missing` names each source not established; `ReadStatus.sourcesMissing` lists sources, never aggregated product strings. Test: `ui_v2_inbox::a_truncated_listing_is_incomplete_coverage_not_a_complete_read` (rows beyond the page → incomplete products and named missing sources; the inventory in one page → ok) | `observation_domain.rs`, `inbox_domain.rs` |
| R3 failed first read shown as pending; failed empty read as all-clear | `ReadState::Failed` precedes "nothing read" (a failed read was attempted); a refresh in which no source answered is not a read (`lastReadAt` stays null, products `failed`/`needsRole` with every source named missing); `ReadStatus.failedAt` added. Home: "Read failed at HH:MM · nothing read yet" or "· showing the read from HH:MM"; Inbox: a failed empty read says so, a failed refresh labels the kept read as older; the completion toast is the warn failure line. Tests: `ui_v2_inbox::a_failed_first_read_is_failed_not_pending_and_a_failed_refresh_keeps_the_older_read`; `inbox.test` failed first read / failed refresh | `inbox_domain.rs`, `home.tsx`, `inbox.tsx`, `copy.ts`, contracts validator |
| R4 arrival and unconfirmed actions global | `Arrival.tenant` (the tenant it was followed in): the shell hands it to a destination only for that tenant and forgets it on a switch; `Unconfirmed.context` (the intent's bound context): entries bound to a retired context are dropped on a context change, never revived or rebound. Test: `inbox.test` (A's API-key arrival and unconfirmed snooze; B inherits neither; back in A's new context the delivery is gone and nothing is re-sent) | `store.ts`, `v2-shell.tsx`, `inbox.tsx`, `home.tsx` |
| R5 discard's removal result discarded | `HistoryJob::Discard` keeps `history::delete`'s result: an absent record is already removed; any other failure is remembered per scope and id, reported as the workspace history's `problem` (when listed, and on later listings) until the operator's own removal succeeds (which clears it); saves of the discarded id stay refused. Test: `harness_tools::a_discard_whose_removal_fails_is_reported_until_the_record_is_removed` (scope folder made read-only; the record stays listed with `problem: unavailable`; made writable, Delete removes it and clears the problem) | `harness_history.rs`, `authority.rs` |
| Optional: workload predicate | `probe activate` takes an optional status prefix; `measure_c30.py` counts the switch shown only once the destination's own cached read status is in the tree (Tenant A "Read finished at", Tenant B "First read pending") | `tools/perf/probe.swift`, `tools/perf/measure_c30.py` |

